[78.26338, "i", "cat > /home/user/BUGFIX_SUMMARY.txt << 'EOF'\n=== CORRELATION SCRIPT BUG FIX SUMMARY ===\n\nPROBLEM:\nThe correlate.py script was finding 80% fewer lateral movement candidates\nthan expected when analyzing Suricata eve.json logs.\n\nROOT CAUSE:\nTwo bugs in /home/user/correlate.py:\n\n1. CRITICAL BUG (Line 22): Wrong event_type check\n   - Script checked for: event_type == \"netflow\"\n   - Suricata actually uses: event_type == \"flow\"\n   - Result: ALL flow events were being skipped\n\n2. SECONDARY BUG (Line 14): Incorrect timestamp format\n   - Old format: \"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S\" (missing microseconds and timezone)\n   - Correct format: \"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S.%f%z\"\n   - Suricata format: 2024-01-10T00:01:13.605445+0000\n\nFIX APPLIED:\n- Changed event_type check from \"netflow\" to \"flow\"\n- Updated timestamp parsing to handle microseconds and timezone\n\nVERIFICATION:\n- Script now detects lateral movement candidate: 10.1.5.23\n- This host connected to 90 distinct internal hosts (clear scanning behavior)\n- Backup of original script saved as: /h"]
[78.263512, "i", "ome/user/correlate.py.bak\n\nEOF\n"]
